# Line endings are load-bearing in this repo.
#
# The working copy lives on an NTFS drive but every script is executed by bash
# inside WSL / Docker / a GitHub Actions runner. A single CRLF in a .sh file
# produces `bash: line 1: $'\r': command not found`, or worse, a shebang that
# silently resolves to nothing. Normalising to LF in the index AND in the
# working tree removes that failure mode for everyone who clones this.
#
# This file must exist before the first `git add`, otherwise already-tracked
# files keep whatever line endings they were committed with.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.c         text eol=lf
*.h         text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.pin       text eol=lf

# Evidence files. Never touch these — a normalised byte is a corrupted capture,
# and byte counts are the unit this project reports its results in.
*.pcap      binary
*.pcapng    binary
*.der       binary
*.bin       binary
*.png       binary
*.pdf       binary

# A signed reference value is CBOR, and a COSE signature covers the exact bytes
# of the protected header and the payload. There is no encoding in which a
# normalised 0x0d is still the document that was signed, so both are binary and
# stated rather than guessed: `text=auto` decides by looking for NUL bytes, and
# a CoRIM small enough to contain none would be silently mangled.
*.cbor      binary
*.corim     binary

# A certificate exists in this repository in two encodings and they are not the
# same kind of file. The .der is the certificate as it goes on the wire, and one
# normalised byte changes the SHA-384 that a capture's RootHash is checked
# against. The .cert is its base64 PEM wrapper, which is text and should be
# normalised like every other text file. Stated rather than left to text=auto's
# NUL-byte heuristic, because "git guessed right" is not a property this repo
# reports numbers on top of.
*.cert      text eol=lf
*.certchain binary

# Keep generated evidence out of diff noise but still reviewable.
docs/env-baseline.md    linguist-generated=true
